==English==
{{wikipedia}}
[[Image:Tampon with applicator.jpg|thumb|A tampon with an applicator]]

===Etymology===
{{defdate|1848}} {{bor|en|fr|tampon|withtext=1}}, from {{etyl|frm|en}} {{m|frm|tampion}}, a nasalised variant of {{m|frm|tapon}}, a diminutive or augmented form of {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|tape||plug, bung, tap}}, from {{etyl|frk|en}} {{m|frk|*tappo||stopper, plug}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{m|gem-pro|*tappô||plug, tap}}. Cognate with Old High German {{m|goh|zapfo||stopper}}, Old English {{m|ang|tæppa||stopper}}. More at {{l|en|tap}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/ˈtæmˌpɒn/|lang=en}}
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|/ˈtæmˌpɑn/|lang=en}}
* {{IPA|[ˈtʰæmpʰɔn]|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[plug]] of [[cotton]] or other [[absorbent]] material [[inserted]] into a [[body cavity]] or wound to [[absorb]] fluid, especially one inserted in the [[vagina]] during [[menstruation]].
# A double-headed [[drumstick]] primarily for the [[bass drum]].
# An [[ink]]ing [[pad]] used in [[lithographic]] [[printing]].

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|intravaginal plug used to absorb menstrual blood}} {{l|en|vampire's teabag}} {{qualifier|slang}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|emotional tampon}}

